    "probe_text": "I now have the complete picture. Here is the ordered list of everything that happens when creating an owner via `POST /api/owners`.\n\n## Gate (whole endpoint)\n\n- **Authorization** \u2014 `authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"`. Without the `OWNER_ADMIN` role the request is denied before any step runs.\n\nThe pipeline then runs 16 steps in sequence (`owners.POST.yml`). Steps from `uniqueIdentity` onward run under `govern: [ transaction ]`, so the whole thing commits once at the end.\n\n## Validations (in order)\n\n1. **`RequireOwnerFields`** \u2014 binds the `@RequestBody`, then:\n   - Normalizes `address` up front (`AddressNormalizer`: trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST\u2192STREET`/`RD\u2192ROAD`/`AVE\u2192AVENUE`). *(side-effect on the body)*\n   - Rejects (**400**, `MissingOwnerFieldsException`) if any of `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone` is null/blank \u2014 listing every missing field. (Address blank is checked *after* normalization.)\n   - Normalizes `telephone` to E.164 (`TelephoneE164`); rejects (**400**, `InvalidTelephoneException`) if it can't form a valid E.164 number (incl. country-specific length rules: +61\u21929 national digits, +1\u219210). *(mutates body)*\n   - If `email` present: trims + lower-cases; rejects (**400**, `InvalidEmailException`) if it fails the syntactic regex; rejects (**400**, `DisposableEmailException`) if the domain is `mailinator.com`/`tempmail.com`/`guerrillamail.com`; stores it lower-cased. If absent, sets `email` to null. *(mutates body)*\n   - Republishes the validated body as a variable.\n\n2. **`RequirePostcode`** \u2014 only if a postcode is present. Must be exactly 4 digits, and for a known city (Sydney/NSW 2000\u20132099, Melbourne/VIC 3000\u20133099, Brisbane/QLD 4000\u20134099) must fall in that range; else **400** `InvalidPostcodeException`. Absent postcode accepted. No mutation.\n\n3. **`RequireUniqueIdentity`** *(transactional)* \u2014 scans all owners; rejects **409** `DuplicateIdentityException` when either:\n   - the new owner's whole `identityKey` (`normalizedTelephone|email|householdId`) equals an existing owner's, or\n   - an existing owner shares the deterministic `householdId` (same lastName + postcode) \u2014 unless the request set `sharesHousehold=true`, which bypasses this second check.\n\n4. **`RequireCityCapacity`** *(transactional)* \u2014 counts owners in the same city (case-insensitive, collapsed whitespace); rejects **409** `CityAtCapacityException` if \u2265 50.\n\n5. **`RequireNotFutureRegistrationDate`** \u2014 only if `registrationDate` supplied; rejects **400** `FutureRegistrationDateException` if it is after today (checked on the raw supplied value).\n\n6. **`DetermineRegistrationDate`** \u2014 computes the *effective* registration date: supplied date or today, rolled forward off weekends to the next Monday. Publishes it as a variable (side-effect: establishes the date every later step uses).\n\n7. **`RequireDailyOwnerLimit`** *(transactional)* \u2014 counts existing owners already registered on that effective business day; rejects **429** `DailyOwnerLimitExceededException` if \u2265 100.\n\n## Side-effects \u2014 building & enriching the owner (all transactional)\n\n8. **`BuildOwner`** \u2014 maps the validated DTO to an `Owner` (`OwnerMapper.toOwner`), then overrides its `registrationDate` with the effective business-day date. Publishes the `Owner`.\n\n9. **`AssignHouseholdId`** \u2014 sets `householdId` = `HH-` + SHA-256(normalized lastName + `|` + postcode) truncated, or null when no postcode.\n\n10. **`AssignCustomerCode`** \u2014 sets `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, where REGION comes from postcode/city (`OwnerLocality`) and HASH8 = first 8 hex of SHA-256(normalizedTelephone + lastName).\n\n11. **`AssignNamesakeCount`** \u2014 sets `namesakeCount` = number of existing owners sharing this first+last name (case-insensitive), before save.\n\n12. **`AssignHouseholdSize`** \u2014 sets `householdSize` = existing owners with the same `householdId`, plus 1 (owners with no householdId \u2192 1).\n\n13. **`AssignBulkSignupWarning`** \u2014 sets `bulkSignupWarning` = true if > 80 owners already exist for the same effective registration day.\n\n14. **`AssignPossibleDuplicate`** \u2014 sets `possibleDuplicate=false` by default; if not a declared household member (`sharesHousehold` not true) and has a householdId, flags `possibleDuplicate=true` and `possibleDuplicateOf=<lowest matching owner id>` when an existing owner shares the household but has a different telephone.\n\n15. **`SaveOwner`** \u2014 `ownerRepository.save(owner)` \u2014 the actual persistence.\n\n16. **`AuditOwnerCreated`** \u2014 logs one line to the `AUDIT` logger (id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel), after save so the id exists.\n\n17. **`RespondWithOwnerCreated`** \u2014 maps to `OwnerDto` and returns **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n### Notes\n- **Ordering rationale baked in:** field/postcode/telephone validation precede the DB uniqueness/capacity checks; the future-date check runs on the raw value *before* `DetermineRegistrationDate` adjusts it; all \"count existing owners\" enrichment steps run *before* `SaveOwner` so the new owner isn't counted against itself.\n- `membershipLevel` is logged by the audit step but is **not** set anywhere in this pipeline \u2014 it comes from `OwnerMapper.toOwner`/the model default, not the create flow.\n- Escalation handlers exist for each thrown exception under `officefloor/escalation/`, mapping them to the status codes above; anything unmatched falls through to Spring's advice."
